, "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2020-08-29T00:01:51Z", "updated_at": "2020-08-29T00:03:11Z", "body": " ```c++\r\n> connection_result = mavsdk.setup_udp_remote(...);\r\n\r\n```\r\nThat actually did work! Thanks!\r\n\r\nThe only difference is if I use `add_any_connection(...)` , the argv would be something like udp://:14540, using `setup_udp_remote(...)` requires the ip and port as separate arguments. \r\n\r\nCorrect me if I am wrong: Once the connection is setup, this udp remote method handle the communication the same as add_any_connection method, right?", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/683196335/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 1, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null, "event": "commented", "actor": {"login": "cjffly", "id": 11035640, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjExMDM1NjQw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11035640?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly", "html_url": "https://github.com/cjffly", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cjffly/subscriptions", "organiza